 ## HEIC/HEIF fallback
 
-Detect HEIF from MIME, case-insensitive `.heic`/`.heif`, or `ftyp` brands. Try native browser decoding first, then lazily load `heic-to/csp` in an on-device Worker. Ordinary JPEG/PNG/WebP inputs do not load it. Use the first image returned by the library; this does not promise full multi-image, video, Live Photo, or HEIF codec support. Invalid/unsupported files produce an error.
+Detect HEIF from MIME, case-insensitive `.heic`/`.heif`, or `ftyp` brands. Try native browser decoding first, then lazily load the locally vendored CSP build of `heic-to` in an on-device Worker. Ordinary JPEG/PNG/WebP inputs do not load it. Use the first image returned by the library; this does not promise full multi-image, video, Live Photo, or HEIF codec support. Invalid/unsupported files produce an error.
 
 The host must honor `worker-src 'self' blob:` from `public/_headers`. First fallback use needs the decoder assets; offline restart behavior and physical-device support require separate verification.
+
+The vendored module is rebuilt from pinned libheif/libde265 C/C++ sources. Ordinary
+`npm run build` checks its source/recipe/output hashes and ships source and rebuild
+materials under `out/source/`, linked from `/notice`. Keep that directory in static
+and Docker deployments. Dedicated `heic:verify`, `heic:verify:source` and
+`heic:verify:relink` commands check native rebuilding and modified-library use; see
+[the recipe](https://github.com/mksdr/Miroven/blob/HEAD/tools/heic/README.md).
+Successful tests do not certify all LGPL distribution conditions.
 
